{
  "paraId": "5B2D1C19",
  "style": "",
  "text": "To the best of our knowledge, this is the first study to generate a weighted pseudo-population by IPW with demographic and clinical characteristics closer to those of the target RA patients in the CREDIT cohort, and to use Bootstrap to estimate the mean and uncertainty of annual RA costs given their right-skewed distribution. The average annual total cost per patient was 41,971 CNY (95%CI: 37,107–47,046 CNY), with direct costs accounting for 75% or more. Medical costs were 28,792 CNY (95%CI: 24,893–33,208 CNY), nearly 89% of direct costs and about half of them medication. Disease activity, hospitalization, comorbidity (e.g., joint replacement or allergy), and biologics or glucocorticoid treatment substantially increased total RA costs, which were also higher in the west than in the central and eastern regions of China. These findings offer a reliable picture of the RA economic burden in real-world clinical practice under treat-to-target strategies in China."
}

